;;; modus-themes.scm -- Emacs's Modus themes: Modus Vivendi (white on
;;; black) and Modus Operandi (black on white), by Protesilaos Stavrou,
;;; made to the highest standard of color contrast (WCAG AAA, 7:1).
;;;
;;;   (use-package! 'modus-themes)
;;;   (load-theme! 'modus-vivendi)
;;;
;;; The colors are Modus's own, copied from modus-themes.el 5.3.0: each
;;; theme's palette names its colors (bg-main, red-warmer, ...) and what
;;; each color is for (keyword, string, bg-region, ...), as a color or
;;; another name. Every imp face takes the color Modus gives the same
;;; thing in Emacs (modus-face-table). Palette overrides change a name,
;;; and every face using it follows.

